{"id": "live-394", "title": "New Securities Suit Against Arbor Realty Trust, Inc. (Problem-Loan Disclosure Claims, E.D.N.Y.)", "category": "reit-securities", "status": "filed", "date": "2026-11-09", "jurisdiction": "United States District Court, Eastern District of New York", "state": "NY", "amount": "$1.25B+ in problem loans and foreclosed properties described in the complaint; no damages figure stated", "source": "live", "source_url": "https://www.investmentnews.com/regulation-legal-compliance/investor-alleges-arbor-realty-trust-misled-market-on-125b-loan-mess/268963", "summary": "A shareholder filed a securities fraud class action against mortgage REIT Arbor Realty Trust, Inc. (NYSE: ABR) and two senior executives on November 9, 2026 in the U.S. District Court for the Eastern District of New York, alleging violations of Section 10(b) of the Securities Exchange Act and SEC Rule 10b-5. The complaint says the company's statements about resolving more than $1.25 billion in problem loans and foreclosed properties misled investors while that pile of distressed assets kept growing.", "significance": "A second securities suit against Arbor Realty Trust over its bridge-loan book, filed after an earlier class action covering 2021-2024 was dismissed in March 2026. Shows that mortgage REITs with large bridge-loan portfolios face repeat securities exposure each time disclosed nonperforming-loan trends diverge from prior projections, independent of how an earlier class period's litigation was resolved.", "judge": null, "tags": ["reit-securities", "mortgage-reit", "bridge-loans", "securities-fraud", "new-york"]}
